it{LC}_\\alpha$", "MATH_0012": "$Y \\in \\textit{LC}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\text{size}(Y) \\leq Bound(\\text{size}(X))$", "MATH_0014": "$Y$", "MATH_0015": "$\\textit{LC}_\\alpha$", "MATH_0016": "$\\text{Cov}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\textit{LC}_\\alpha$", "MATH_0018": "$\\textit{LC}_\\alpha$", "MATH_0019": "$(\\textit{LC}_\\alpha, \\text{Cov})$", "MATH_0020": "$\\textit{LC}_{qc}$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{remark-set-theoretic-LC}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-equation-bound}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sets-lemma-construct-category}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sets-lemma-coverings-site}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}[", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e6c09bc2c92be6e6c88fe08992fcb3050ee1939d641ab3e2e6f40bc51ea0fa52", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:ec3dcd03e8b6b8afd1e597d29495b72365b4206eb8b3f22f4c2916bb511afc2b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b719cef4be8e94ca04de79432e05f80e9a87ad62ebc63798fb53a36ce1797557", "source_text": "Set theoretic issues<OWNARGEND_0001>The category <MATH_0001> is a ``big'' category as its objects form\na proper class. Similarly, the coverings form a proper class.\nLet us define the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>size<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of a topological space <MATH_0002> to be the\ncardinality of the set of points of <MATH_0003>. Choose a function\n<MATH_0004> on cardinals, for example as in\nSets, Equation (<REF_0001>).\nFinally, let <MATH_0005> be an initial set of objects of <MATH_0006>,\nfor example <MATHSEG_0001>euclidean topology<MATHSEG_0002>.\nExactly as in Sets, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwe can choose a limit ordinal <MATH_0007> such that\n<MATH_0008>\ncontains <MATH_0009> and is preserved under all countable limits and\ncolimits which exist in <MATH_0010>. Moreover, if <MATH_0011>\nand if <MATH_0012> and\n<MATH_0013>, then <MATH_0014> is isomorphic\nto an object of <MATH_0015>.\nNext, we apply Sets, Lemma <REF_0003>\nto choose set <MATH_0016> of qc covering on <MATH_0017>\nsuch that every qc covering in <MATH_0018> is\ncombinatorially equivalent to a covering this set.\nIn this way we obtain a site <MATH_0019>\nwhich we will denote <MATH_0020>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:530c59509f767946908a5961aedcc1d5926d4cfac42b6be69beea398c1c26b08", "unit_id": "tag:09X2:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "09WY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\textit{LC}_{qc}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\textit{LC}_{qc}$", "MATH_0005": "$X_i \\to X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{LC}_{Zar}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\textit{LC}_{Zar} \\to \\textit{LC}_{qc}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\epsilon : \\textit{LC}_{qc} \\longrightarrow \\textit{LC}_{Zar}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$X \\in \\Ob(\\textit{LC}_{qc})$", "MATH_0011": "$$\n\\epsilon_X : \\textit{LC}_{qc}/X \\longrightarrow \\textit{LC}_{Zar}/X\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$X_{Zar}$", "MATH_0013": "$X$", "MATH_0014": "$$\n\\pi_X : \\textit{LC}_{Zar}/X \\longrightarrow X_{Zar}\n$$", "MATH_0015": "$X_{Zar} \\to \\textit{LC}_{Zar}/X$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\mapsto U$", "MATH_0017": "$X_{Zar}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\pi$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\pi_X : \\Sh(\\textit{LC}_{Zar}/X) \\longrightarrow \\Sh(X)\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$\\Sh(X_{Zar}) = \\Sh(X)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-set-theoretic-LC}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{section-compare}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-lemma-localize-morphism}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-example-site-topological}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{sites-proposition-get-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1bc51c6dbbc3bc282d10ee3325844f6fe17b71723290ce76894f120d14467081", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ebbd63445e478293ea1b883cbeda92429f9d46d28698ba6cb164b2e9ac7dd669", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThere is a second topology on the site <MATH_0001> of\nRemark <REF_0001>. Namely, given an object\n<MATH_0002> we can consider all coverings <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>\nsuch that <MATH_0005> is an open immersion. We denote this site\n<MATH_0006>. The identity functor\n<MATH_0007> is continuous and defines\na morphism of sites\n<MATH_0008>\nSee Section <REF_0002>.\nFor a Hausdorff and locally quasi-compact topological space <MATH_0009>, more\nprecisely for <MATH_0010>, we denote the induced morphism\n<MATH_0011>\n(see Sites, Lemma <REF_0003>).\nLet <MATH_0012> be the site whose objects are opens of <MATH_0013>, see\nSites, Example <REF_0004>.\nThere is a morphism of sites\n<MATH_0014>\ngiven by the continuous functor\n<MATH_0015>, <MATH_0016>.\nNamely, <MATH_0017> has fibre products and a final object and the\nfunctor above commutes with these and\nSites, Proposition <REF_0005> applies.\nWe often think of <MATH_0018> as a morphism of topoi\n<MATH_0019>\nusing the equality <MATH_0020>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f68e3563a91a813f8a4bcc1fcbf1370d321a52d3598aa28031bb934014ce0bcd", "unit_id": "tag:09WY:prose-0006"}
